        The companion of the opaque type `S32`, exported with it to the `hypotenuse` package.
    entry .Min   `-2147483648`
    entry .Max   `2147483647`
    entry .underlying   evidence that an `S32` is an `Int` underneath
    entry .addable   `S32 + S32`, from the `CheckOverflow` policy in scope
        `overflow.addS32`; under `checkedOverflow`, `S32.Max + S32(1)` and `S32.Min +
        S32(-1)` raise `Arithmetic.Error`.
    entry .subtractable   `S32 - S32`, from the `CheckOverflow` policy in scope
    entry .multiplicable   `S32 * S32`, from the `CheckOverflow` policy in scope
        The product is computed in a `Long` and, under `checkedOverflow`, checked to fit an
        `Int`.
    entry .divisible   `S32 / S32`, truncating, from the `DivisionByZero` policy in scope
    entry .canEqual   an `S32` may be compared with `==` to any signed, floating or primitive numeric type
    entry .fromDigits   an `S32` from an integer literal, under `genericNumberLiterals`
    entry .textualizable   renders the signed decimal value as `Text`
    entry .apply   `S32(bits: B32)`: reads a bit pattern as a signed integer
    entry .orderable   signed comparison for `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `min` and `max`
